# upstream/103-sparse-region-successors-protected: a sparse forward
# analysis may override visitRegionSuccessors and hand the successors it
# leaves to the base. An integer range analysis that counts its calls and
# hands each to the base runs, and the scf.if's result has the range
# [1, 2]: built against the toolchain's MLIR, statically, the program
# prints "ok". At the pin the base is private and it does not build.
# Building a program against MLIR's libraries takes longer than a step.
step_limit=180
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
mlir_check "an override of visitRegionSuccessors runs and hands each successor to the base" \
  "$root/upstream/103-sparse-region-successors-protected/override.cpp"
